// Data of the note on "Continuous control with deep reinforcement learning" (Lillicrap et al., ICLR 2016), DDPG, on the
// rally with any speed. Written by course-materials/reinforcement-learning/scripts/ddpg/note/write-site-data.mjs (outside
// the repository) from the checked outputs of gen-data.mjs (the opening and section 1) and gen-train.mjs (sections 2-6),
// seed 3 of the note's run and the reruns' runs. Do not edit by hand: rerun the scripts, which also rewrite the version in
// deep-deterministic-policy-gradient.js's import of this file. Every number below was computed by a script; none is typed.
//
// speeds: the 41 speeds a = −1 + 0.05 j of the critic's curves.
// open, ac: frames[t] = [bx, by, dx, dy, py, a, r, ev]: the state at frame t (t = 0 is the serve); a = mu(s_t), the actor's speed read at this frame (the speed played from it; the last frame's is not played); r = the reward of the step that led to this frame (0 at the serve); ev = 0 nothing, 1 hit, -1 miss, 2 serve. A perfect episode ends at the 10th hit (the cut).
//   open.pause = [t*, first arrival + 1]; ac.pause = [t*]. t* = first arrival - 4 (ball on column 10 moving right).
//   ac.curve[t][j] = Q(s_t, a_j | theta^Q), a_j = -1 + 0.05 j (j = 0..40), eval mode, to 3 decimals, t = curveFrom..curveTo (the serve to the second arrival). muQ[t], slope[t]: Q and dQ/da at a = mu(s_t), 4 decimals. yRange: the curve's min and max over those frames, rounded out to 0.1.
//   ac.tries[mode][j], the try of speed a_j from frame t*: tops = the paddle's top at frames t*+1 .. first arrival; acts = the speed of each of those frames' moves (acts[0] = a_j, from t*); outcome 1 hit, -1 miss; cost = sum of 0.05 a^2 over those frames (4 decimals). held: a_j at every frame; oneFrame: a_j for one frame, then mu plays on.
// train.reels: A training reel: frames[i] = [bx, by, dx, dy, py, a, r, ev, t]: the state before training step t (1-based), a the speed taken from it (the clipped actor's speed plus noise), r and ev the reward and event of the step that led to this frame (0 and 2 at the serve; ev 1 hit, -1 miss). The last frame is the state after the episode's last step, with a 0 (not played) and t that step's number. mu[i] and noise[i]: the actor's speed and the noise of frame i's step. The memory holds t steps once step t is stored.
//   A greedy reel: part 1's frames, [bx, by, dx, dy, py, a, r, ev], a the trained actor's speed, no noise.
// train.s2: pauseA at the frame of step 2,000, whose update is shown: remembered is the drawn step k (stored at step k) with the largest |y - Q| among the drawn hits; qBefore and qAfter are Q(s_k, a_k) in eval mode before and after the critic's step; d = qAfter - qBefore; pct = |d| / |y - qBefore|. pauseB: the first frame after step 2,000 with the ball on column 10 moving right whose one-frame tries (that speed for one frame, then the actor of that moment) give at least 5 hits and 5 misses; trueValue[j] = the discounted return of one frame of speed j then that actor without noise, to the end of the episode. lead: the training episodes from the one running at step 1,000 to the one before seq, played first in fast-forward. ff: the critic's curve for the remembered frame s_k (step k) at every 8th step (rows[i] at step from + 8i: the critic of that step's frame, before its update), at the 21 speeds -1 + 0.1 j, in thousandths; yRange covers them, both curves of the update and y.
// train.s3: meanQ[i]: the mean of Q(s_i, a_i) over the minibatches of the 1,000 steps before check i (checksT), from the reruns; null at step 0. qMax = 1/(1 - 0.95^28), the most any frame can be worth, counting on play to go on as the critic's targets do; qMin = -1.05, a miss on the next frame at the fastest speed.
// train.s4, s5, s6: { reel, frame }: a frame index in that reel. Curves: Q at the 41 speeds of about.speeds, eval mode, 3 decimals. yRange: rounded out to 0.1.
